    "kind": "abridged",
    "full_paras": [
     "If ever my soul tasted true gladness, it was when, by Your Paternity's reply received through the Father Rector, I conceived a sure hope that I too must one day follow in the footsteps of those who labor with such zeal for the aid of the Indies. And how often I think of it — I do so very often through the day — I know not what sweetness I feel, which to my mind can be none but of Paradise. I have wished many times to make it known to Your Paternity, and my not having done so was a certain respect which I now condemn. And indeed, to tell the truth, I feel myself stirred by holy emulation of those whom this very day I have heard are already summoned for so fortunate a sending. O Our Father, by me most dearly loved, kneeli